## Tauri command surface

All frontend I/O goes through `src/lib/tauri.ts` → `invoke()`. In browser dev (no Tauri),
`src/lib/devMockApi.ts` provides mock data.

### Games & settings

| Command | Args | Returns | Notes |
| ------- | ---- | ------- | ----- |
| `list_games` | — | `Game[]` | Full library |
| `get_game` | `gameId` | `Game \| null` | Single record |
| `create_game` | `request: CreateGameRequest` | `Game` | Manual add |
| `update_game` | `gameId`, `request: UpdateGameRequest` | `Game` | Edit properties |
| `toggle_favorite` | `gameId` | `Game` | |
| `set_game_hidden` | `gameId`, `hidden` | `Game` | |
| `delete_game` | `gameId` | `void` | Blocked if game is actively running |
| `clear_library` | — | `number` | Count removed; blocked if session active |
| `get_setting` | `key` | `T \| null` | e.g. `themeId`, `rawgApiKey` |
| `set_setting` | `key`, `value` | `void` | JSON-serialized in SQLite |

### Sessions & window

| Command | Args | Returns | Notes |
| ------- | ---- | ------- | ----- |
| `launch_game` | `gameId` | `GameSession` | Spawns process via `launching/` |
| `stop_game` | `sessionId` | `GameSession` | User-initiated stop |
| `get_active_session` | — | `GameSession \| null` | |
| `set_window_fullscreen` | `fullscreen` | `void` | |
| `hide_orbit_window` | — | `void` | During gameplay |
| `show_orbit_window` | — | `void` | After session ends |

### Importers

| Command | Args | Returns | Notes |
| ------- | ---- | ------- | ----- |
| `detect_importers` | — | `ImporterStatus[]` | Steam, Astris, native, GameHub |
| `scan_steam_library` | — | `ScanResult` | Upserts + optional auto-enrich for new IDs and games missing artwork; all scans guarantee artwork in every slot |
| `scan_astris_folder` | `folder` | `ScanResult` | User-selected folder |
| `scan_native_apps` | — | `ScanResult` | macOS `/Applications` |
| `scan_gamehub_folder` | `folder?` | `ScanResult` | GameHub shortcuts; auto-enrich when Steam app ID present |
| `import_game_path` | `path` | `ScanResult` | Manual file/folder pick |

### Themes & artwork

| Command | Args | Returns | Notes |
| ------- | ---- | ------- | ----- |
| `list_custom_themes` | — | `ThemeDefinition[]` | From Application Support; sanitized (invalid themes skipped, unsafe images dropped) |
| `save_custom_theme` | `theme` | `ThemeDefinition` | Theme studio; id must be `custom-<slug>`; writes `<id>.json` and returns the sanitized theme |
| `delete_custom_theme` | `id` | `()` | Removes `custom-<slug>.json`; missing files are not an error |
| `themes_directory` | — | `string` | Path to custom themes folder |
| `read_artwork_from_path` | `path` | `string` | Base64 image |
| `fetch_artwork_from_url` | `url` | `string` | Base64 image |
| `search_public_artwork` | `query` | `ArtworkResult[]` | RAWG (optional key) + Wikimedia |
| `search_game_artwork` | `query`, `slot` (`cover`/`hero`/`icon`/`logo`), `gameId?`, `source?` (`all`/`steamgriddb`) | `{ hits: ArtworkResult[], warnings: string[] }` | Queries every configured provider independently; per-provider failures become warnings. `steamgriddb` restricts to the exact-matched SteamGridDB game (used by Random) |
| `enrich_game_metadata` | `gameId` | `{ enriched, message }` | TheGamesDB metadata + SteamGridDB / TheGamesDB artwork |
| `enrich_games_metadata` | `gameIds` | `{ enriched }` | Batch used after import |
| `get_metadata_cache_stats` | — | `{ gameCount, dbPath }` | Local metadata cache size |
| `test_metadata_api_keys` | — | `{ thegamesdbOk, steamgriddbOk, message }` | Settings connection test |

TypeScript shapes: `src/types/game.ts`, `src/themes/types.ts`.
Rust models: `src-tauri/src/models/`.

