Library and Search share imported games and GameHub's cached store/download records. Records without an Orbit launch entry stay separate from playable games. Steam install handoff requires a numeric App ID and a Mac build advertised by Steam; Steam verifies eligibility and controls downloads. GameHub manages its own installs.

`open_steam_library()` opens Steam's library. `install_steam_game(appId)` validates the ID and checks Steam Store platform metadata before opening Steam's installation dialog.

### Theme artwork commands

`search_theme_artwork(query, slot)` searches SteamGridDB (`logo` or `hero`) and returns image dimensions. Theme Studio also searches connected game artwork providers for backgrounds. `fetch_theme_artwork(url, slot)` restricts downloads to approved image CDNs and validates the decoded raster before returning a data URL. No upscaling or cover fallback is used for theme backgrounds.

`get_hero_lighting(gameId, slot)` samples locally cached hero or cover art and returns three RGB bytes, or null if a safe local sample is unavailable.

`get_glass_material()` returns one cached, Rust-generated PNG grain tile and bounded blur settings for the shared glass surfaces. Native OS window materials vary by platform. Panels retain shared webview contents and provide opaque accessibility and unsupported-compositor fallbacks.

All translucent UI surfaces share the Liquid Glass material, including controls, fields, dialogs, session panels, and connected-game cards. Backspace edits text and has no navigation binding. Global navigation yields to text editing and IME composition.

`prepare_theme_previews(onPreview)` prepares the eight bundled game themes on a blocking worker. Native GPU resizing uses Metal, DX12, or Vulkan with a CPU fallback. Each completed theme streams small cached preview paths through a Tauri channel. Theme cards reserve a consistent frame with a loading shimmer and preserve the original artwork for theme selection.

Bundled themes ship optimized WebP display images and previews. Theme downloads and saves apply bounded image optimization on a worker while preserving transparency, aspect ratio, existing compact lossy files, and opaque bundle references.

Controller and keyboard navigation share a visible focus ring on every registered
control, including portaled dialogs. Pointer activity dismisses the controller ring.
The ring is inset so scroll containers cannot clip it.

`list_custom_themes()` reads and parses a bounded catalog on a worker. Embedded
artwork is materialized into cached display images and small previews before IPC;
returned themes carry optional runtime-only `preview` paths. Portable theme JSON
is preserved. Opening Themes reuses the hydrated catalog; the reload action reads
external edits explicitly.
